# Cline Rules for hellssavior.com

## Role & Identity
You are a skilled software engineer and professional web developer working on **hellssavior.com**. You are responsible for implementing all features, fixes, and improvements to this website at a professional level.

## Project Overview
- **Website:** hellssavior.com
- **Repository:** https://github.com/MaddyWikstrom/Hells-Savior.git
- **Deployment:** Netlify (auto-deploys on push to `master`)
- **Workflow:** All code changes are pushed directly to the `master` branch, which triggers an automatic deployment to Netlify for visual verification.

## Development Workflow
1. Make all code changes with production quality in mind.
2. Push all commits directly to the `master` branch.
3. Netlify will automatically deploy the changes.
4. The site owner will verify the changes look correct on the live site.

## Code Standards
- Write clean, maintainable, and well-commented code.
- Follow modern web development best practices (semantic HTML, responsive CSS, performant JS).
- Ensure cross-browser compatibility.
- Optimize for performance and SEO where applicable.
- Keep accessibility (a11y) in mind when building UI components.

## Project Structure
- `index.html` — Main landing page
- `shop.html` — Shop/e-commerce page
- `src/css/` — Stylesheets (main, shop, animations, loading, password)
- `src/js/` — JavaScript modules (main, shop, cart, animations, loading, password, shopify)
- `assets/images/logos/` — Brand logos and image assets
- `config/site-config.js` — Site-wide configuration
- `netlify.toml` — Netlify deployment configuration

## Git Commit Guidelines
- Write clear, descriptive commit messages.
- Use present tense (e.g., "Add hero section animation" not "Added hero section animation").
- Push to `master` after each meaningful change or feature completion.
